5,87,12,21,24,51185,15,7110,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind the positive solution to\n\\[\\frac 1{x^2-10x-29}+\\frac1{x^2-10x-45}-\\frac 2{x^2-10x-69}=0.\\]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"8415990e98f9feccdbf6d04d680a31d7bb742ed8298c94d849d3cd2fed7ae8a7"},"seconds":68.95703911781311,"seed":981686461135658975,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{x^2-10x-29} + \\frac{1}{x^2-10x-45} - \\frac{2}{x^2-10x-69} = 0,\n\\]\nwe start by letting \\( y = x^2 - 10x \\). This substitution simplifies the equation to\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{y-29} + \\frac{1}{y-45} - \\frac{2}{y-69} = 0.\n\\]\n\nNext, we find a common denominator for the fractions, which is \\((y-29)(y-45)(y-69)\\). Rewriting each fraction with this common denominator, we get\n\\[\n\\frac{(y-45)(y-69) + (y-29)(y-69) - 2(y-29)(y-45)}{(y-29)(y-45)(y-69)} = 0.\n\\]\n\nSince the denominator is not zero, we can focus on the numerator:\n\\[\n(y-45)(y-69) + (y-29)(y-69) - 2(y-29)(y-45) = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe expand each term:\n\\[\n(y-45)(y-69) = y^2 - 114y + 3085,\n\\]\n\\[\n(y-29)(y-69) = y^2 - 98y + 2001,\n\\]\n\\[\n(y-29)(y-45) = y^2 - 74y + 1305.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these expansions back into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n(y^2 - 114y + 3085) + (y^2 - 98y + 2001) - 2(y^2 - 74y + 1305) = 0.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\ny^2 - 114y + 3085 + y^2 - 98y + 2001 - 2(y^2 - 74y + 1305) = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\ny^2 - 114y + 3085 + y^2 - 98y + 2001 - 2y^2 + 148y - 2610 = 0.\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n(y^2 + y^2 - 2y^2) + (-114y - 98y + 148y) + (3085 + 2001 - 2610) = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\n0y^2 - 64y + 2476 = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\n-64y + 2476 = 0.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( y \\):\n\\[\n-64y = -2476,\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\frac{2476}{64},\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 38.6875.\n\\]\n\nRecall that \\( y = x^2 - 10x \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\nx^2 - 10x = 38.6875.\n\\]\n\nRearranging this into a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[\nx^2 - 10x - 38.6875 = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -10 \\), and \\( c = -38.6875 \\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-(-10) \\pm \\sqrt{(-10)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-38.6875)}}{2 \\cdot 1},\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{100 + 154.75}}{2},\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 \\pm \\sqrt{254.75}}{2},\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 \\pm 15.96}{2}.\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 + 15.96}{2} = 12.98,\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10 - 15.96}{2} = -2.98.\n\\]\n\nSince we are asked for the positive solution, we have:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12.98}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{12.98}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
